# Exercise: Float Comparisons
#
# Float comparison operators (word forms also available, e.g., f.gt, f.lt):
#   f.=   ( a b -- bool )   Equal
#   f.<>  ( a b -- bool )   Not equal
#   f.<   ( a b -- bool )   Less than
#   f.>   ( a b -- bool )   Greater than
#   f.<=  ( a b -- bool )   Less or equal
#   f.>=  ( a b -- bool )   Greater or equal
#
# Seq also supports type-inferred comparison operators:
#   =, <>, <, >, <=, >=  (work for both integers and floats)
#
# Examples:
#   3.14 2.0 f.>    # true (3.14 i.> 2.0)  (explicit float)
#   3.14 2.0 >      # true (3.14 i.> 2.0)  (inferred float)
#   1.0 1.0 f.=     # true (explicit float)
#   1.0 1.0 =       # true (inferred float)
#
# Your task: Compare 5.5 and 3.0. Is 5.5 greater than 3.0?
# The result should be true.
# When done, delete the marker line below.

